This Terraform program creates a CloudWatch metric alarm named "foobar" that triggers when the CPU utilization of an EC2 instance exceeds 80%. The alarm sends notifications to an SNS topic. A Route 53 health check is also created to monitor the endpoint, using the CloudWatch metric alarm as the trigger. The health check is configured to use HTTP requests to the instance's root path (`/`) and checks every 30 seconds, with a failure threshold of 3 consecutive failures before considering the instance unhealthy.

